    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated <span class="ph">[go-live date]</span> · <a href="/da/privatliv" hreflang="da">Dansk version</a></p>
    <p class="draft"><b>Draft for legal review.</b> Placeholders are highlighted. Describes Kupro as built in October 2026, with
      transcripts deleted when a meeting ends.</p>

    <section class="short" aria-labelledby="short-h">
      <h2 id="short-h">The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We collect what we need to run your account and your workspace. Nothing for advertising.</li>
        <li>Everything is stored and processed in the EU, by EU companies.</li>
        <li>Meeting audio is never stored. Transcripts are deleted when the meeting ends, unless your workspace chooses to keep them.</li>
        <li>We don't use your data to train AI models, and neither do our vendors.</li>
        <li>We use no tracking cookies. You can see, export and delete your data.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
    <p>Kupro is run by Pilgaard Development, CVR 41249269, Nordlyvej 20, 8550 Ryomgård, Denmark.
      Questions about privacy go to <a href="mailto:contact@kupro.app">contact@kupro.app</a>. We answer within 30 days, usually much sooner.</p>

    <h2 id="roles">Your data or your company's</h2>
    <p>Kupro holds two kinds of personal data, and the rules differ.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Data about you as a user</b>: your account, how you sign in, invoices, support emails and security logs. We decide how
        this is used, so we are the <i>data controller</i>. This policy covers it.</li>
      <li><b>Data inside a workspace</b>: issues, comments, attachments, meeting transcripts and everything else your team puts in. The
        company that owns the workspace decides what goes in and who sees it. They are the controller and we are their
        <i>data processor</i>, bound by our <a href="/dpa">data processing agreement</a>. Questions about that data go to your
        workspace owner first; we help them answer.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="what">What we collect</h2>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Where it comes from</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Account</td><td>You, when you sign up or are invited</td><td>Name, email, password (stored only as a hash), language, time zone</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Workspace membership</td><td>You and your workspace owner</td><td>Workspaces you belong to, your role, hours per week for capacity planning</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Agents and tokens</td><td>You</td><td>Agent names you create, API tokens and when they were last used</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Workspace content</td><td>You and your team</td><td>Issues, comments, attachments, activity history. We process this for your company (see above)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Billing</td><td>The workspace owner</td><td>Company name, CVR/VAT number, billing email, invoices. Card details go straight to the card acquirer; we never see them</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Security and operations logs</td><td>Your browser, the CLI or an MCP client</td><td>IP address, time, which request, errors, sign-in attempts</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Support</td><td>You, when you write to us</td><td>Your email and what you tell us</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2 id="meetings">Meeting agent</h2>
    <p>The meeting agent is off until someone in your workspace starts a meeting session. While it runs:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your browser records short pieces of speech, a few seconds each, and sends them to our servers.</li>
      <li>We send each piece to Scaleway in Paris for transcription, then drop the audio. <b>Audio is held in memory only and
        never written to disk.</b></li>
      <li>We send the text, with the titles of issues that might be relevant, to a language model at Scaleway to suggest issue changes.</li>
      <li>The transcript is kept while the meeting runs, so the agent can follow the conversation. Each suggestion shows the few
        words that triggered it, so you can see why it was proposed. <b>When the meeting ends, the transcript and those words are
        deleted.</b> If nobody ends the meeting, they are deleted after a day.</li>
      <li>A workspace owner can choose to keep transcripts for up to 365 days instead, for example to look back at a planning
        meeting. Everyone in a session then sees how long the transcript is kept.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout">Everyone in a session sees that it is listening. If people who are not Kupro users are in the meeting, the
      workspace owner is responsible for telling them and, where needed, asking for their consent. The person who starts the
      session can pause or stop it at any time.</p>

    <h2 id="why">Why we may use it</h2>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Create your account, sign you in, run the service you or your company signed up for</td><td>Contract, Art. 6(1)(b)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Send emails the service needs: invites, password resets, notifications you turned on</td><td>Contract, Art. 6(1)(b)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Keep the service secure, stop abuse, find and fix errors</td><td>Legitimate interest, Art. 6(1)(f): a service that works and isn't misused</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Invoices and bookkeeping</td><td>Legal obligation, Art. 6(1)(c): the Danish Bookkeeping Act</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Answer support questions</td><td>Contract or legitimate interest, depending on the question</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Product emails about new features (only if you opt in)</td><td>Consent, Art. 6(1)(a). Unsubscribe from any email</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2 id="keep">How long we keep it</h2>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Kept for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Meeting audio</td><td>A few seconds, in memory only</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Meeting transcript and the words behind each suggestion</td><td>Until the meeting ends, or up to 365 days if the workspace owner chooses</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Workspace content</td><td>Until the workspace owner deletes it, or 30 days after the subscription ends</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Account</td><td>Until you delete it. Your name stays on changes you made in a workspace's history; ask the owner or us to replace it with "Former member"</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Security and operations logs</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Backups</td><td>35 days, then overwritten</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Invoices and billing records</td><td>5 years from the end of the financial year, as Danish law requires</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Support emails</td><td>12 months after the conversation ends</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2 id="share">Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>We use a small number of EU companies to run Kupro. They process data only on our instructions, under a data
      processing agreement. The full list, with what each one does, is on the <a href="/subprocessors">sub-processors page</a>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>OVHcloud</b> (France): servers, database, file storage and backups, in EU data centres.</li>
      <li><b>Scaleway</b> (France): sending email, and transcription and suggestions for the meeting agent.</li>
      <li><b>Alunta</b> (Denmark) and our card acquirer <span class="ph">[OnPay or QuickPay, chosen before billing starts]</span> (Denmark): subscriptions and payments.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't transfer personal data outside the EU/EEA. Our source code is hosted on GitHub; no customer data is stored there.
      We share data with public authorities only when Danish or EU law requires it.</p>

    <h2 id="not">What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No advertising, no selling or renting data, no data brokers.</li>
      <li>No tracking cookies or third-party analytics. See the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>.</li>
      <li>No training of AI models on your data. Scaleway processes meeting audio and text to return a result. It doesn't keep
        what we send or use it to train or improve models. The one exception: if traffic harms their service, Scaleway may keep
        the affected requests for up to two weeks to investigate. It keeps anonymous usage statistics (such as request counts)
        for up to 6 months.</li>
      <li>No automated decisions with legal or similar effect on you. Meeting suggestions are applied only when your workspace allows it, and can always be undone.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
    <p>Data is encrypted in transit (TLS). Passwords are hashed by Keycloak, the open-source sign-in server we host ourselves. Access to
      production is limited to the founders and protected with two-factor authentication. Each workspace's data is
      separated in the database, and every query is checked against the workspace you are signed in to. If a breach affects your data,
      we tell the workspace owner without undue delay, and Datatilsynet within 72 hours where the law requires it.</p>

    <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us to show you the data we hold about you, correct it, delete it, limit how we use it, or give it to you in a
      machine-readable format. You can object to processing based on legitimate interest. Write to <a href="mailto:contact@kupro.app">contact@kupro.app</a>.
      For data inside a workspace, we pass your request to the workspace owner and help them handle it.</p>
    <p>Much of this you can do yourself: edit your profile in the app, export a workspace (owners), or delete your account.</p>
    <p>If you think we handle your data wrongly, you can complain to the Danish Data Protection Agency: Datatilsynet, Carl Jacobsens Vej 35,
      2500 Valby, <span class="mono">dt@datatilsynet.dk</span>, datatilsynet.dk. We would like the chance to fix it first.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>When we change this policy in a way that matters, we email workspace owners at least 30 days before it takes effect and
      show a note in the app. Earlier versions are available on request from <a href="mailto:contact@kupro.app">contact@kupro.app</a>.</p>
